                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8887b75-fd50-3d3c-9b16-a4950c4a8d33",
                                        "entry_id": "a762a434-f594-39d1-85df-c279381139ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who strolls."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da94ca56-fed7-3e5d-bbcc-0cdade8a1765",
                                        "entry_id": "a762a434-f594-39d1-85df-c279381139ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vagrant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea347d1c-2724-461b-8343-b6ca7293fd39",
                                                "sense_id": "da94ca56-fed7-3e5d-bbcc-0cdade8a1765",
                                                "text": "The mayor observed that it was great presumption in Wilson, who was a stroller, to proceed to such extremities with a gentleman of family and fortune; and threatened to commit him on the vagrant act."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89ec5a7b-ba59-37ee-8074-f2c501a17e6b",
                                        "entry_id": "a762a434-f594-39d1-85df-c279381139ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Men's semiformal daytime dress comprising a grey or black single- or double-breasted coat, grey striped or checked formal trousers, a grey or silver necktie, and a grey, black or buff waistcoat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5d65f2d1-5aff-45d5-b86d-04db36fb8f87",
                        "source_entry_id": "5c6069fe-6e39-32c4-be10-429aef0e23a8",
                        "source_sense_id": "d558206b-cc90-3e2b-ac29-d21daf1f222c",
                        "target_lang_word": "loiterer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loiterer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a08cd64-3212-3890-bc9e-391fc9fd9b4b",
                                        "entry_id": "ae94b0a9-cc55-3970-abf1-453e2d236d79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who loiters, one who lingers or hangs around."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b56a30e0-0c4f-488b-9895-6787ed7a7170",
                                                "sense_id": "9a08cd64-3212-3890-bc9e-391fc9fd9b4b",
                                                "text": "Though unusual in the Dublin area he knew that it was not by any means unknown for desperadoes who had next to nothing to live on to be abroad waylaying and generally terrorising peaceable pedestrians by placing a pistol at their head in some secluded spot outside the city proper, famished loiterers of the Thames embankment category they might be hanging about there or simply marauders ready to decamp with whatever boodle they could in one fell swoop at a moment's notice, your money or your life, leaving you there to point a moral, gagged and garrotted."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8c19b19-082f-40bb-a488-3b357eebcaa4",
                                                "sense_id": "9a08cd64-3212-3890-bc9e-391fc9fd9b4b",
                                                "text": "[…] currently incarcerated Stinc Team members Ketchy the Great, SaySoTheMac, and Bambino; the devilish and gravelly Almighty Suspect; red-clad Inglewooder and headband connoisseur FreeAckrite; baby-faced Martin Luther King Park loiterer Johnny Rose; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8ee99d31-5b9e-4186-ae15-eb8cd615d075",
                        "source_entry_id": "5c6069fe-6e39-32c4-be10-429aef0e23a8",
                        "source_sense_id": "d558206b-cc90-3e2b-ac29-d21daf1f222c",
                        "target_lang_word": "layabout",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "layabout",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b55b0b05-9ec8-3c7b-8fb4-86fe4e499560",
                                        "entry_id": "efac0369-9db5-3e39-86b2-4988163b4c80",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lazy person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3407c68f-02e8-4b6b-b38e-484cb100103d",
                                                "sense_id": "b55b0b05-9ec8-3c7b-8fb4-86fe4e499560",
                                                "text": "“That’s better. Gilbert Goodie! I should have known it was you. The one-legged layabout. The uni-ped idler. The stumpy skiver. Stealing coins from a wishing well now, are we? You couldn’t make it up!”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eff13397-cbe8-4ce1-a288-76cb2ca57647",
                        "source_entry_id": "5c6069fe-6e39-32c4-be10-429aef0e23a8",
                        "source_sense_id": "d558206b-cc90-3e2b-ac29-d21daf1f222c",
                        "target_lang_word": "flaneur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "flaneur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b2280a7-63b3-3a85-8dc2-39c2b632efe9",
                                        "entry_id": "5d06a8fc-0d74-3791-9800-07ec6a7745fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who wanders aimlessly, who roams, who travels at a lounging pace. One who walks to observe and enjoy rather than to get somewhere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97fe9e9b-be04-4371-a27d-afd82b49cf75",
                                                "sense_id": "2b2280a7-63b3-3a85-8dc2-39c2b632efe9",
                                                "text": "[…]Bevil drew him up to the door-step of a house close by, where, on certain evenings, a well-known club drew together men who seldom meet so familiarly elsewhere—men of all callings; a club especially favoured by wits, authors, and the flaneurs of polite society."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be82ef34-f138-4472-9046-8aa07383e350",
                                                "sense_id": "2b2280a7-63b3-3a85-8dc2-39c2b632efe9",
                                                "text": "It often seemed to Mallet that he wholly lacked the prime requisite of a graceful flâneur—the simple, sensuous, confident relish of pleasure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1811ca09-4829-480e-8151-edc2e1da5f10",
                                                "sense_id": "2b2280a7-63b3-3a85-8dc2-39c2b632efe9",
                                                "text": "Indeed I lost patience altogether, and asked myself by what right this informal votary of form pretended to run riot through a poor charmed flaneur’s quiet contemplations, his attachment to the noblest of pleasures, his enjoyment of the loveliest of cities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08b24c4d-4393-48a9-9a4a-0d4adf4d8c85",
                                                "sense_id": "2b2280a7-63b3-3a85-8dc2-39c2b632efe9",
                                                "text": "More than any other urban type, the flaneur suggests the contradictions of the modern city, caught between the insistent mobility of the present and the visible weight of the past."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48f1b5f1-3c28-49f6-953e-705729eaf673",
                                                "sense_id": "2b2280a7-63b3-3a85-8dc2-39c2b632efe9",
                                                "text": "Portsmouth is a flaneur’s dream come true, a place that simply begs to be explored randomly and on foot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "662f84ea-4bf6-44bc-9539-14d196735196",
                                                "sense_id": "2b2280a7-63b3-3a85-8dc2-39c2b632efe9",
                                                "text": "In observing Dublin in this way – its cultural and geographic context, its streets and skies, neighbours and wider world – Whitney is occupying consciously the role of flâneur, defined by Baudelaire as \"a lounger or saunterer, an idle man about town\", a gatherer of aesthetic impressions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c34e1623-7a10-3432-9b8d-4b9e974d9381",
                                        "entry_id": "5d06a8fc-0d74-3791-9800-07ec6a7745fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An idler, a loafer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1efa167-1161-4995-a773-15966c2a2b01",
                                                "sense_id": "c34e1623-7a10-3432-9b8d-4b9e974d9381",
                                                "text": "The Byrons and Brookes who had defied life from mountain tops were in the end but flaneurs and poseurs, at best mistaking the shadow of courage for the substance of wisdom."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "flaneur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed514d39-7cc5-3896-97a9-f7161890b184",
                                        "entry_id": "2e24f39e-1249-3929-93f9-aece184afa65",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To wander aimlessly or at a lounging pace. To walk to observe and enjoy rather than to get somewhere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f9df87c-9f57-4077-9951-ae662daa6382",
                                                "sense_id": "ed514d39-7cc5-3896-97a9-f7161890b184",
                                                "text": "Meantime, we flaneured about the Guernsey market, and a remarkable pretty sight it was this bright morning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "114874ab-b22f-42dc-a50e-fcac14c337ae",
                                                "sense_id": "ed514d39-7cc5-3896-97a9-f7161890b184",
                                                "text": "Still, I wrote him often, and although I missed him, through autumn I contentedly flaneured about. At Alchemy's Christmas break we flew to Paris and stayed at Nathaniel's flat on Rue du Cherche-Midi. The three of us would lahdidah to the Luxembourg Gardens, where we read Alchemy the French canon of subversive lit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0beb713b-2f6f-4b36-84f3-312c65970823",
                                                "sense_id": "ed514d39-7cc5-3896-97a9-f7161890b184",
                                                "text": "Flaneuring, at its essence, is the art of wandering aimlessly through urban environments, observing the world with a curious and open mind. It's about savoring the journey rather than fixating on a destination."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d4ae46b-de6e-4ab4-8c42-ef365885815e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5c6069fe-6e39-32c4-be10-429aef0e23a8",
